[{:db/id 17592186179731 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b6d2ac1d-75ed-5453-8dc7-92123acc1f15" "question-15dd7515-4c6a-53a1-ac3c-ffc4846bc122"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b6d2ac1d-75ed-5453-8dc7-92123acc1f15" :question/id #uuid "b6d2ac1d-75ed-5453-8dc7-92123acc1f15" :question/math-academy-id "q-124308" :question/problem "![](images/fb/fb482ddbb5bde83cfd6ed383b0f321cb27377f34aafcb9e74e44d91824dcf366.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is the path comprising of a line segment and a semicircle of radius $1,$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${x}_{2}=-3$ and ${x}_{1}=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1}=(-3)-2=-5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-39828f92-e829-5bba-b1e4-9d6adfcd1f10"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-39828f92-e829-5bba-b1e4-9d6adfcd1f10" :answer-field/id #uuid "39828f92-e829-5bba-b1e4-9d6adfcd1f10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-77030057-915a-5bf2-b853-884b00d3a0fe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c85b8a30-49c9-5708-b7f3-202e64369872" "answer-77030057-915a-5bf2-b853-884b00d3a0fe" "answer-1832c026-532a-5b68-9cf9-1e99d898f97f" "answer-a4fa88c2-055c-5698-ac15-9fab33508e53" "answer-aa2086cd-91f8-5e89-a8cf-09b5f2f54c73"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c85b8a30-49c9-5708-b7f3-202e64369872" :answer/id #uuid "c85b8a30-49c9-5708-b7f3-202e64369872" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77030057-915a-5bf2-b853-884b00d3a0fe" :answer/id #uuid "77030057-915a-5bf2-b853-884b00d3a0fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1832c026-532a-5b68-9cf9-1e99d898f97f" :answer/id #uuid "1832c026-532a-5b68-9cf9-1e99d898f97f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi +3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4fa88c2-055c-5698-ac15-9fab33508e53" :answer/id #uuid "a4fa88c2-055c-5698-ac15-9fab33508e53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa2086cd-91f8-5e89-a8cf-09b5f2f54c73" :answer/id #uuid "aa2086cd-91f8-5e89-a8cf-09b5f2f54c73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi +3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-15dd7515-4c6a-53a1-ac3c-ffc4846bc122" :question/id #uuid "15dd7515-4c6a-53a1-ac3c-ffc4846bc122" :question/math-academy-id "q-124328" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d4d60c547afdb873c30e6c5e1f70d616dc31ace79b482f37ae51ea4f036d5a42.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the closed path along the quarter circle of \nradius $2,$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, the initial and terminal points are the same (since the path is closed and is traversed only once). Therefore, ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$ and we have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-00fb8aa7-71b4-5be7-ac8f-e5b17414c65f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-00fb8aa7-71b4-5be7-ac8f-e5b17414c65f" :answer-field/id #uuid "00fb8aa7-71b4-5be7-ac8f-e5b17414c65f"